// KNOWN SILENT-WRONG (open) — the monomorphization residue:
// Hβ.emit.spec-nested-lambda-twin. NOT gated: compiles clean, runs wrong.
//
// A LAMBDA inside a named generic body does the arithmetic. The demand
// analysis correctly twins the named function (the scan descends into
// closure bodies, so $scale_all$sp22 exists), but the lambda is a SEPARATE record
// emitted once at the word floor, and the twin's LMakeClosure still
// references the floor lambda's table index — so the multiplication runs
// i32.mul on the f64 references and ys is garbage (exit 1, zero
// diagnostics). Landed shapes are sound: named-body arithmetic (sum_acc),
// named comparators higher-order (reduce(xs, min)), the transitive web
// (sort → merge), and lambdas authored AT a concrete call site (main's own
// map lambda — specialized where it is born). Only a lambda BORN INSIDE a
// generic body inherits the floor.
//
// The fix is the same mechanism one level deeper: a worthy twin's nested
// closure records join the demand set under the same wide type, and the
// twin's body is rewritten to reference the lambda-twin's index (a pure
// LowExpr rename walk). Scoped out of the first landing deliberately —
// none of the harvested silent-wrong shapes needed it; this probe
// (2026-07-22) is its first witness. Turn into a frontier gate (expect 42)
// when the lambda-twin lands.
fn scale_all(xs, k) = map((x) => x * k, xs)

fn main() = {
  let ys = scale_all([1.5, 2.5], 2.0)
  if ys[0] == 3.0 && ys[1] == 5.0 { 42 } else { 1 }
}
